$f(x)$ defined by $f(x) = 2x-3,$ find $f^{-1}(x).$</p>\n","choice1":"$f^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{x+3}{2}$","choice2":"$f^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{x-3}{2}$","choice3":"$f^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{x-2}{3}$","choice4":"$f^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{x+2}{3}$","choice5":"$f^{-1}(x) = {3x-2}$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\\[\ny = 2x-3\n\\]</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\\[\nx = 2y-3\n\\]</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Solve for $y$:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\nx &= 2y-3 \\\\[5pt]\nx + 3 &= 2y \\\\[5pt]\n\\dfrac {x + 3} {2} &= y \\\\\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p><strong>Step 4:</strong> Replace $y$ with $f^{-1}(x)$:\n\\[\nf^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac {x + 3} {2}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":627,"name":"Calculating the Inverse of a Function"},"example":{"id":3968,"title":"Finding the Inverse of a Linear Function"},"group":{"id":9229,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14229433,"answer":{"id":62203570,"cread":"2026-10-15T06:16:10.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15459},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62203588,"created":"2026-10-15T06:16:25.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":"[\"\\\\frac{7-x}{3}\"]","timeElapsed":11876,"number":2,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 6:16 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":218691,"format":"FR","difficulty":1,"exampleId":3968,"text":"If $f(x) = -3x + 7$, then $f^{-1}(x) =$","choice1":" ","choice2":" ","choice3":" ","choice4":" ","choice5":" ","freeAnswerChoice":"[\nanswer: \\dfrac{7-x}{3};\ntype: expression;\nwidth: 55;\nmargin-left: 4;\nmargin-right: 1;\nbuttons: frac;\n].","explanation":"<p>To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\\[\ny = -3x+7\n\\]</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\\[\nx = -3y+7\n\\]</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Solve for $y$:\n\\begin{align*}\nx &= -3y+7 \\\\[5pt]\n3y &= 7-x \\\\[5pt]\ny &=\\dfrac {7-x } {3} \\\\\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p><strong>Step 4:</strong> Replace $y$ with $f^{-1}(x)$:\n\\[\nf^{-1}(x) =  \\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{\\dfrac{7-x}{3}}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":627,"name":"Calculating the Inverse of a Function"},"example":{"id":3968,"title":"Finding the Inverse of a Linear Function"},"group":{"id":77059,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14229433,"answer":{"id":62203588,"cread":"2026-10-15T06:16:25.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":["\\frac{7-x}{3}"],"timeElapsed":11876},"graphic":false,"freeResponse":{"segments":[{"textbox":{"answer":"\\dfrac{7-x}{3}","type":"expression","width":55,"margin":{"left":4,"right":1},"buttons":["frac"]}},{"text":"."}]},"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":3970,"number":2,"title":"Finding the Inverse of a Function With a Parameter","answers":[{"id":62203621,"created":"2026-10-15T06:16:47.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13956,"number":3,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 6:16 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":35323,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":3970,"text":"<p>Find the inverse of the function $f(x) = 4x+3b$, where $b$ is a constant.</p>\n","choice1":"$f^{-1}(x)= \\dfrac{x - 3b}{4}$","choice2":"$f^{-1}(x)= \\dfrac{x - 4b}{3}$","choice3":"$f^{-1}(x)= \\dfrac{x + 3b}{4}$","choice4":"$f^{-1}(x)= \\dfrac{x + 4}{3b}$","choice5":"$f^{-1}(x)= 3x- 4b$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\\[\ny = 4x+3b\n\\]</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</s